      "content": "Abstract A, authored by Dr. Alistair Sterling, presents a more authoritative study for a peer reviewer due to the specific mentioning of the author's name. Including the author's credentials adds weight to the credibility of the research and gives a clearer context for the author's expertise, which strengthens the perception of intellectual authority and rigor. Abstract B, while conveying a similar message, omits the author's details and thus feels less authoritative in comparison, despite covering the same content.",
